---
title: "4 · Prepare the contract"
description: Choose the client, the signatory, the issuing entity, the language and the format, and enter the values of the payment schedule.
sidebar:
  order: 11
  label: "4 · Prepare the contract"
---

**Who:** the person in charge. **Where:** the opportunity › **Contract** tab › step 1 **Prepare**.

The **Contract** tab opens on the list of the opportunity's contracts. Select **Create contract from services** to start a new one. Each contract has its own number. While a contract is in progress (not yet signed or void), a second one cannot be started.

## Client

Choose **Company** or **Individual**.

- **Company:** the UEN and the address come from the company's record in **Clients**. A missing value is marked **Missing — add it to the record before generating**. Pick the **Client signatory**. If the services are for another company, choose it under **Company the services are for**: **Same as client**, **Another company in CRM**, or **Proposed name (not yet incorporated)**.
- **Individual:** the details you enter are saved as a person under **Clients** › **People** with **Save to People**.

{% aside type="note" title="Who can be the client signatory" %}
Only people who can sign for the company are offered: a current director, chairman, partner, sole proprietor, manager, corporate representative or contact person of the company in **Clients**. Shareholders, the secretary, nominee directors and vendors are not offered. If the list is empty, first add a director or manager on the company's **Relationships** tab in **Clients** (see [Relationships](/en/clients/relationships/#add-a-role)); any staff member can do this.
{% /aside %}

## Contract

Choose the country (the opportunity's country by default), the **Issuing entity**, the **Language** and the **Format** (**Engagement letter**, **Quotation** or **VIP contract**). Together they select the template.

Only combinations with a registered template are offered. If the country has none, the page says so; ask a tenant admin to register one (see [1 · Contract settings](/en/crm/templates/)). An issuing entity that lacks a bank account in the contract's currency is marked **Setup incomplete**.

{% screenshot id="crm/prepare-form" caption="The Prepare step: client, signatory, issuing entity, language and format." /%}

{% screenshot id="crm/prepare-entities" caption="Only issuing entities with a template are offered." /%}

## Signs for the firm

Under the step bar, **Signs for the firm** shows who signs the contract for the firm: the contract signatory of the opportunity's **Director in charge**. If no one can sign, the reason and the fix are shown, for example:

- the opportunity has no Director in charge: set it on the opportunity's **Details** tab;
- the Director in charge is not a contract signatory, or may not sign for the chosen issuing entity: a tenant admin adds or changes the record under **Contract signatories** (**Open CRM settings**).

Without a signatory the contract cannot be generated or sent. Without an active saved signature it can be generated, but not sent.

## Services and prices

The services and prices are read from the **Services** tab. To change them, select **Edit in Services**. Services already in a signed contract are not included: a contract made after signing holds only the services added since.

## Payment schedule

Under the services, when a service is paid in installments or has a refund clause, the **Payment schedule** shows each installment with its share and amount. Enter the values asked for, for example the **Refund percentage (%)** or the **Refund deduction amount**, or the amount of an extra fee. A value marked **Required before generating** must be entered before the contract can be generated.

{% screenshot id="crm/prepare-payment-schedule" caption="The payment schedule: two installments and the refund percentage for this contract." /%}

## Generate

When every choice is made, select **Generate contract**. If something is missing, the reason is shown next to the button. The page moves to step 2 **Draft** (see [5 · Generate and check the draft](/en/crm/draft/)).
